// Jenkinsfile_Lynn_Sahyouni - Lab 10, Part 4
// Setup -> Lint -> Test -> Coverage -> Security Scan -> Deploy
// The Jenkins agent is Windows, so every step uses `bat` and calls the
// virtual environment's python.exe directly instead of activating it.
pipeline {
    agent any

    environment {
        VIRTUAL_ENV = 'venv'
        VENV_PY = 'venv\\Scripts\\python.exe'
        // Python launcher on the Windows agent; 3.13 is the stable interpreter installed there.
        PYTHON_LAUNCHER = 'py -3.13'
        REPORTS = 'reports'
        // Outside the workspace, so cleanWs() does not remove the deployed application.
        DEPLOY_ROOT = "${env.USERPROFILE}\\Lab10_Deploy\\Python-CI-CD"
    }

    stages {
        stage('Setup') {
            steps {
                script {
                    if (!fileExists("${env.WORKSPACE}\\${VIRTUAL_ENV}\\Scripts\\python.exe")) {
                        bat "${PYTHON_LAUNCHER} -m venv ${VIRTUAL_ENV}"
                    }
                }
                bat "${VENV_PY} -m pip install --disable-pip-version-check -r requirements.txt"
                bat "if not exist ${REPORTS} mkdir ${REPORTS}"
            }
        }

        stage('Lint') {
            steps {
                // Checks app.py, deploy.py and tests; venv, reports and caches are excluded in .flake8
                bat "${VENV_PY} -m flake8 ."
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                bat "${VENV_PY} -m pytest -v --junitxml=${REPORTS}\\junit.xml"
            }
        }

        stage('Coverage') {
            steps {
                // .coveragerc measures app.py and deploy.py with branch coverage
                bat "${VENV_PY} -m coverage run -m pytest -q"
                bat """
                    ${VENV_PY} -m coverage report --fail-under=90 > ${REPORTS}\\coverage.txt
                    set COVERAGE_RC=%ERRORLEVEL%
                    type ${REPORTS}\\coverage.txt
                    exit /b %COVERAGE_RC%
                """
                bat "${VENV_PY} -m coverage xml -o ${REPORTS}\\coverage.xml"
                bat "${VENV_PY} -m coverage html -d ${REPORTS}\\htmlcov"
            }
        }

        stage('Security Scan') {
            steps {
                // Any unsuppressed Bandit finding returns a non-zero exit code and fails the build.
                bat """
                    ${VENV_PY} -m bandit -r app.py deploy.py tests -f txt -o ${REPORTS}\\bandit.txt
                    set BANDIT_RC=%ERRORLEVEL%
                    type ${REPORTS}\\bandit.txt
                    exit /b %BANDIT_RC%
                """
                bat "${VENV_PY} -m bandit -r app.py deploy.py tests -f json -o ${REPORTS}\\bandit.json"
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            steps {
                bat "${VENV_PY} deploy.py --deploy-root \"${DEPLOY_ROOT}\" --build-id %BUILD_NUMBER% --commit %GIT_COMMIT% --report ${REPORTS}\\deploy_verification.txt"
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            archiveArtifacts artifacts: 'reports/**', allowEmptyArchive: true
            junit testResults: 'reports/junit.xml', allowEmptyResults: true
        }
        unsuccessful {
            // Collect environment details to help diagnose a failed stage.
            bat(label: 'Collect diagnostics', returnStatus: true, script: """
                if not exist ${REPORTS} mkdir ${REPORTS}
                (echo Build %BUILD_NUMBER% commit %GIT_COMMIT% & where git & py -0p & dir /b /s ${REPORTS} & ${VENV_PY} -m pip list) > ${REPORTS}\\diagnostics.txt 2>&1
                type ${REPORTS}\\diagnostics.txt
            """)
            archiveArtifacts artifacts: 'reports/diagnostics.txt', allowEmptyArchive: true
        }
        cleanup {
            cleanWs()
        }
    }
}
